<title>FRANCE: French farmers protest cheap produce from Spain.</title>
<headline>French farmers protest cheap produce from Spain.</headline>
<dateline>TOULOUSE, France 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>About 100 French farmers protesting against cheap imports from Spain dumped dozens of cases of fruit outside the offices of Prime Minister Lionel Jospin in his southwestern constituency of Cintegabelle on Tuesday, witnesses said.</p>
<p>Police intervened in the early hours of the morning to disperse the demonstrators. The farmers then went to the motorway linking the towns of Toulouse and Narbonne, where they intercepted a truck carrying melons from Spain and destroyed the cargo.</p>
<p>Lower-priced imports of fruit and vegetables from countries like Spain and Portugal have hurt French produce farmers, who have been forced to lower their prices to be more competitive.</p>
</text>
